{
    "background_story": "Josie was a master artisan in the small village of Brindlemark, renowned for her exceptional skill as a guilder. With a steady hand and an eye for detail, she transformed ordinary objects into breathtaking works of art. Her workshop was a treasure trove of gold leaf, precious stones, and fine metals, which she carefully applied to create intricate designs. Josie's most famous commission was a golden reliquary for the village church, adorned with delicate filigree and precious gems. Her work was so exquisite that it attracted the attention of the kingdom's royal family, who requested her expertise in gilding the palace's grand ballroom. Josie's talent and dedication earned her the title of Royal Guilder, and her work continued to inspire awe and wonder throughout the land.",
